# Supabase
.branches

# CLI scratch state — version probes, pooler URL, storage-migration marker. The CLI rewrites these
# on almost every invocation, so tracking them means a conflict on every branch that runs it: 13
# commits here have touched .temp, and 12 of them carried nothing but churn.
#
# `project-ref` is the deliberate exception and MUST stay tracked: deploy-cloud.yml, cloud-smoke.yml
# and verify-edge-env.sh all read it on a FRESH checkout to resolve the Supabase project, and it is
# no longer mirrored in a CI secret. Untracking it breaks production deploys. It is also the one
# file here that does not churn — a single commit in the repo's whole history.
#
# Note the glob must be `.temp/*`, not `.temp`: git does not descend into an ignored DIRECTORY, so
# a bare `.temp` would make the negation below unreachable.
.temp/*
!.temp/project-ref

# dotenvx
.env.keys
.env.local
.env.*.local
